<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="hero hero-lg hero-home">
  <h1>AI Inference on Intel Arc GPUs <br>
    <span class="text-gradient hero-home-tagline">Benchmarks and tested recipies</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The inference engines llama.cpp and vLLM, as well as the Vulkan and SYCL backends, are tested and the results are documented, making the choice easy for you. The <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> is documented so that you can replicate results or contribute.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="primary-btn" href="/results">Browse results</a>
    <a class="secondary-btn" href="/submit">Submit a result</a>
  </div>
</div>

<% if (bestRuns.length > 0) {
  const genRates = bestRuns.map(function(r) { return r.generation_tok_s; });
  const bestGen = Math.max.apply(null, genRates);
  const cardCount = new Set(bestRuns.map(function(r) { return r.card; })).size;
%>
  <div class="stat-row stat-row-lg">
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="stat-value"><%= bestRuns.length %></span>
      <span class="stat-label">configurations benchmarked</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="stat-value"><%= fmt.num(bestGen) %> tok/s</span>
      <span class="stat-label">best generation throughput</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="stat-value"><%= cardCount %></span>
      <span class="stat-label">card<%= cardCount === 1 ? '' : 's' %> tested</span>
    </div>
    <% if (stats.bestEfficiency != null) { %>
      <div class="stat">
        <span class="stat-value"><%= fmt.num(stats.bestEfficiency, 2) %></span>
        <span class="stat-label">best tok/s per watt</span>
      </div>
    <% } %>
    <div class="stat">
      <span class="stat-value"><%= stats.verifiedCount %></span>
      <span class="stat-label">verified submission<%= stats.verifiedCount === 1 ? '' : 's' %></span>
    </div>
  </div>
<% } %>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Benefits of the Arc Ecosystem</h2>
  <p class="section-note">Most people learn toward NVIDIA cards for their CUDA stack, but the Intel cards have many benefits that may make them the better choice.</p>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature-card">
      <h3>Cost per gigabyte of VRAM</h3>
      <p>
        The massive demand for AI compute has driven costs for all RAM extraordinarily high, making it impossible for many local AI enthusiasts with less to spend to get involved in the hobby. Intel has some of the best cards for VRAM/$, bringing cards with 32gb like the B65 to a price where it does become an option for far more people, and it makes it more affordable for clusters as well.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <h3>Rapid development of the stack</h3>
      <p>
        CUDA has been considered the golden standard for years, but Intel's SYCL library is rapidly becoming faster and more reliable, as the Vulkan backend also performs better on Intel GPUs as Mesa, the Linux kernel, and inference enginenes ship bug fixes and performance improvements. The capabilities of these cards will continue to improve, making them a great choice.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <h3>Growing usage in the community</h3>
      <p>
        The local AI community has come to recognize the value of Intel's offering, and is increasingly purchasing and supporting the Intel cards, leading to more development support in the applications involved in the running and hosting of local AI. This means more people sharing the work they're doing on these cards, and a supportive community for those willing to join.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Best result per configuration</h2>
  <p class="section-note">
    Best run for each card × backend × runtime combination, taken at a fixed
    reference workload — concurrency <%= referenceCell.concurrency %>,
    <%= referenceCell.prompt_tokens %>-token prompt — so the six rows are
    comparable with each other rather than each being whichever cell happened
    to score highest. Model varies by row and is named below; use the
    <a href="/results">results table</a> to compare at other workloads.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="matrix-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Card</th>
          <th>Backend</th>
          <th>Runtime</th>
          <th>Model</th>
          <th>Gen tok/s</th>
          <th>Prompt eval tok/s</th>
          <th>tok/s per W</th>
          <th>VRAM used</th>
          <th>Stability</th>
          <th>Trust</th>
          <th></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% bestRuns.forEach(function(r) { %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= r.card %></td>
            <td><%= r.backend %></td>
            <td><%= r.runtime %></td>
            <td><%= r.model_name %></td>
            <td class="num"><%= fmt.num(r.generation_tok_s) %></td>
            <td class="num<%= fmt.missingClass(r.prompt_eval_tok_s) %>"><%= fmt.num(r.prompt_eval_tok_s) %></td>
            <td class="num<%= fmt.missingClass(r.tok_s_per_watt) %>"><%= fmt.num(r.tok_s_per_watt, 2) %></td>
            <td class="num<%= fmt.missingClass(r.vram_used_mb) %>"><%= fmt.unit(r.vram_used_mb, 'MB') %></td>
            <td><span class="badge badge-ok">stable</span></td>
            <td><%- include('partials/trust-badge', { level: r.verification_level }) %></td>
            <td><a href="/configs/<%= r.card %>/<%= r.backend %>/<%= r.runtime %>">Details →</a></td>
          </tr>
        <% }) %>
        <% if (bestRuns.length === 0) { %>
          <tr><td colspan="11">No verified results yet.</td></tr>
        <% } %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<% if (bestRuns.length > 0) { %>
<section class="section">
  <h2>Generation throughput at a glance</h2>
  <p class="section-note">Best run per configuration, side by side.</p>
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="best-runs-chart" height="110"
      data-chart="<%- fmt.chartAttr(bestRuns.map(function(r) {
        return { label: r.card + ' / ' + r.backend + ' / ' + r.runtime + ' — ' + r.model_name,
                 generation_tok_s: r.generation_tok_s, tok_s_per_watt: r.tok_s_per_watt };
      })) %>"></canvas>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.4/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<script src="/js/charts-index.js"></script>
<% } %>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Go deeper</h2>
  <div class="link-card-grid">
    <a class="link-card" href="/results">
      <span class="link-card-index">01</span>
      <h3>Full results table</h3>
      <p>Every verified run — filter by card, backend, runtime, quant, and concurrency; sort on any metric.</p>
      <span class="link-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
    <a class="link-card" href="/methodology">
      <span class="link-card-index">02</span>
      <h3>Methodology</h3>
      <p>The test matrix, what's held constant across runs, and what each metric actually measures.</p>
      <span class="link-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
    <a class="link-card" href="/submit">
      <span class="link-card-index">03</span>
      <h3>Submit a result</h3>
      <p>Add your hardware to the matrix — a copyable prompt lets your own AI agent fill in the details.</p>
      <span class="link-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
